<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John III, Count of Namur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1429">1429</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John III was the last Count of Namur of the house of Dampierre. Heavily in debt and without legitimate heirs, he sold the county to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a>, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, in 1421, keeping its use for life. On his death in 1429 Namur passed to Burgundy and joined the Burgundian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p></div>
